# The env file of the minimal example application: where everything is on this computer, for
# slicerweb.py, build.py and scripts/publish_*.py. Copy it to .env in this folder - .gitignore
# keeps that out of the repository - and set the paths of this computer. Nothing built goes in a
# checkout: everything goes to SW_DIST, also what npm installs (the web application is built,
# served and tested in a copy of web/ there). A relative path is relative to this folder, and an
# environment variable of the same name overrides a line. No secrets here: they go in the files of
# SW_SECRETS.
#
# slicerweb.py works on the folder it is run in, or the one -C <folder> names:
#
#     cd examples/minimal
#     python ../../slicerweb.py build
#     python ../../slicerweb.py build extensions
#     python ../../slicerweb.py build extensions SegmentEditorExtraEffects
#     python ../../slicerweb.py serve
#     python ../../slicerweb.py dev
#     python ../../slicerweb.py test tests/browser-smoke.mjs
#
#     python C:/D/SlicerWeb/slicerweb.py -C C:/D/SlicerWeb/examples/minimal build    # from any folder

# The SlicerWeb checkout that builds the application (default: the one slicerweb.py is in)
#SW_SLICERWEB=C:/D/SlicerWeb
# Where everything built goes: wheels, extensions, the web application, sample data. Each
# application has its own: a build has the extensions of its application only.
SW_DIST=D:/SlicerWeb-build/dist-minimal
# A folder of secrets: github-token, read access to private extensions (optional)
#SW_SECRETS=D:/SlicerWeb-build/secrets/minimal
# The Docker volume of the build trees of SW_SLICERWEB (default slicerweb-build). Each SlicerWeb
# checkout needs one of its own (a build refuses a volume another checkout built in); the
# applications built with the same checkout share it.
#SW_BUILD_VOLUME=slicerweb-build
# The port of serve (default 4175)
#SW_PORT=4175
# The port of dev, the development server of the web application (default 5173)
#SW_DEV_PORT=5173
# 1: serve and dev use https, with a certificate made for this computer, which a headset needs to
# reach them over Wi-Fi (its browser warns about it once)
#SW_HTTPS=1

# For build.py and the publish scripts, run by themselves:
# The folder of extension description files 80-extensions builds (default: those of application.json)
#SW_EXTENSIONS_DIR=C:/D/SlicerWebExtensions
# The repository whose release publish_runtime.py uploads to (default: that of the application)
#SW_RUNTIME_REPOSITORY=myorg/my-app
